<title>UK: Imperial Tobacco up on Rezla acquisition.</title>
<headline>Imperial Tobacco up on Rezla acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Imperial Tobacco rose 9p to 393-1/2p by 1020 GMT after the company announced the 185 million stg acquisition of handrolled tobacco paper group Rizla International BV of the Netherlands.  </p>
<p>Dealers said the takeover of Rizla, the world's largest maker of handrolled tobacco papers, was welcomed by the investment community because it appeared to enhance Imperial's earnings and expansion potential.</p>
<p>&quot;People seem to think it was a good move,&quot; said one.</p>
<p>Imperial was demerged from Hanson Plc in October.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
